<p>
  Inventory keeps count of the goods you buy and sell, where they are, and what they're worth.
</p>

<h2>Tracking a product</h2>
<p>
  Open a product of type <strong>Goods</strong>
  under <.link navigate="/products">Products</.link>
  and switch on <strong>Track stock on hand</strong>. Optionally set a <strong>reorder level</strong>: when stock falls to
  that quantity, it's flagged <em>Low</em>. Services are never stocked.
</p>

<h2>How stock moves</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>When you…</th><th>Stock</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Receive a purchase order</td><td>
        Goes up in the order's warehouse (a <em>GRN</em> receipt)
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Approve a bill without an order</td><td>Goes up in the default warehouse</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Deliver a sales order</td><td>Goes down (a <em>DO</em> delivery)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Issue an invoice not delivered by an order</td><td>Goes down</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Void a bill or invoice</td><td>Is put back the way it was</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Adjust stock</td><td>Goes up or down by what you enter (an <em>ADJ</em> adjustment)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>
  Every movement is listed under <.link navigate="/inventory/operations">Movements</.link>, and each
  product's page shows its full history.
</p>

<h2>Goods received and delivery notes</h2>
<p>
  Every receipt prints as a <strong>goods received note</strong>
  and every delivery as a <strong>delivery note</strong>: who it's from or to, the warehouse, the order, the reference, the
  items and quantities (no prices), a tick box per line and signature lines. Open the movement and
  click the print button, or use the printer icon next to it on the order.
</p>

<h2>Stock counts and adjustments</h2>
<p>
  Counted the shelves and found a difference? Click <strong>Adjust stock</strong>
  on the <.link navigate="/inventory">Stock</.link>
  page and enter the change: <code>+5</code>
  if you found more, <code>-2</code>
  for damaged or lost items, with a short reason. A wrong adjustment can be reversed by an
  admin from its page.
</p>

<h2>What your stock is worth</h2>
<p>
  Zippiker values stock at <strong>weighted average cost</strong>. Buy 10 at $5 and 10 at $7 and each one is
  worth $6. Goods leave at that average, so the cost of what you sold lands in your profit &amp; loss
  automatically.
</p>

<h2>Several warehouses</h2>
<p>
  Add shops, depots or vans under <.link navigate="/inventory/warehouses">Warehouses</.link>. Choose
  which one an order ships from or a purchase order arrives in; filter the stock page by warehouse.
  The <strong>default</strong> warehouse is used when you don't choose.
</p>
<.callout>
  Stock can go below zero if you sell before receiving. It shows in red so you can catch up on
  receiving.
</.callout>
